# Actual built-in generation prompt

Use case: scientific-educational. Create one original SkillPilot chemistry learning-goal illustration as a friendly abstract colorful comic illustration, PNG landscape, about 1600 x 900 pixels (16:9; a nearby native size is acceptable). It supports the goal 'Den Weg einer Wirkstoffgruppe von der Forschung zur Vermarktung erschließen'. A single calm composition with four large clearly connected stages, few bold shapes and plenty of space, readily understandable when the complete image is only 360 pixels wide. Stage one: a scientist with safety glasses comparing two sample containers and a simple data card; no readable tiny data. Stage two: a small safe supervised laboratory setup, with a clearly separate compact glass reaction vessel behind a protective screen; no procedural recipe. Stage three: a larger closed stirred production vessel, visibly jacketed for cooling, followed by a separate simple product-separation container; this is a schematic contrast of laboratory and industrial scale, not a realistic engineering plan. Stage four: an unbranded medicine box with a folded information leaflet and a plain price tag, examined by a person; no patient taking a medicine, no sales or treatment recommendation. Repeat the same subtle sample color across stages to connect them. Three large forward arrows make the main route clear, and one unobtrusive curved feedback arrow returns a production observation toward research. The artwork should look warm, approachable and hand drawn, matching a school chemistry comic collection: rounded shapes, dark blue outlines, gentle teal/orange accents, softly off-white background. Text: only four short, large, exact German labels 'Forschung', 'Labor', 'Produktion', 'Vermarktung'. No other writing, no molecular or reaction formulas, no doses, no real brand names, no promises of healing, no money-profit imagery, no approval ticks. Depicted people and objects must have consistent viewpoints; nobody reads a card or instrument backwards. No photorealism, no sterile technical diagram, no SVG. Do not present commercialization as proof of safety or efficacy. No existing image is an edit target; this is a new illustration for a genuinely missing goal.
